## 🚀 Quick Checklist

- [ ] Project scaffolded (Next.js + Tailwind)
- [ ] Core components built (ProductCard, CartIcon, etc.)
- [ ] API client set up
- [ ] State management wired (Redux Toolkit)
- [ ] Routing configured
- [ ] Accessibility reviewed
- [ ] Performance optimizations applied
- [ ] Tests written & passing
- [ ] CI/CD pipeline in place
- [ ] Deployed to CDN

---

### Final Thought

Building a robust e‑commerce frontend is a marathon, not a sprint. Start small—get a single product page working end‑to‑end—then iterate. Keep the code modular, test frequently, and always keep the user experience at the forefront. Happy coding!
